{"qid":"Q2361927","names":["Duchy of Masovia"],"title":"Duchy of Masovia","endonym":{"native":"Księstwo mazowieckie","lang":"pl"},"capsule":"The Duchy of Masovia was a Piast principality occupying the middle Vistula basin (modern central Poland including Warsaw), created when Masovia was separated from the Polish duchy in 1138 under the testament of Bolesław III Wrymouth, which fragmented Poland among his sons. The duchy was progressively diminished by transfers of its northern territories—Conrad of Masovia's invitation to the Teutonic Knights in 1226, ceding Chełmno Land as their base—and by piecemeal reincorporation into the Polish Crown; the last Masovian Piasts died without heirs in 1526, after which the duchy was formally incorporated into the Crown of Poland.","attestation":"Boundaries from Seshat Cliopatria (Bennett et al., Scientific Data 2025; CC BY 4.0), digitized from standard historical atlases at ~0.07° resolution. The Piast charters and Polish chronicles establish Masovia's political history clearly; territorial boundaries within the fragmented Piast realm fluctuated considerably and spatial reconstructions rely on administrative documents of uneven survival.","attestationLinks":[{"label":"Cliopatria dataset (Seshat, CC BY 4.0)","url":"https://github.com/Seshat-Global-History-Databank/cliopatria"},{"label":"Bennett et al. 2025, Scientific Data","url":"https://www.nature.com/articles/s41597-025-04516-9"}],"citations":[{"label":"Britannica: Masovia","url":"https://www.britannica.com/place/Masovia"},{"label":"Wikipedia: Duchy of Masovia","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Duchy_of_Masovia"}],"britannica":null,"cowCode":null,"wikipedia":"Duchy of Masovia","rulers":[{"qid":null,"name":"Bolesław I of Masovia","nativeName":"Bolesław I mazowiecki","roman":"Bolesław I","start":1138,"end":1173,"image":null,"imageUrl":null,"imageLicense":null},{"qid":null,"name":"Leszek I of Masovia","nativeName":"Leszek I mazowiecki","roman":"Leszek I","start":1173,"end":1186,